      {
        "question_text": "a. The digits give $24\\times5=120$. Find $0.24\\times0.5$.\nb. The digits give $25\\times8=200$. Find $0.025\\times0.08$.",
        "solution_text": "a. $0.24$ has $2$ decimal places and $0.5$ has $1$.\n$2+1=3$ decimal places, so $120$ becomes $0.120$.\nRemove the trailing zero: $0.24\\times0.5=0.12$.\nb. $0.025$ has $3$ decimal places and $0.08$ has $2$.\n$3+2=5$ decimal places, so $200$ becomes $0.00200$.\nRemove the trailing zeros: $0.025\\times0.08=0.002$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "The digits give $432\\times6=2592$. Find $4.32\\times6$.",
        "solution_text": "$4.32$ has $2$ decimal places and the whole number $6$ has none.\n$2+0=2$ decimal places.\nPlace the point in $2592$ to give $2$ decimal places.\n$4.32\\times6=25.92$"
      }
    ],
